    10	
    11	## Key Insights Mapped to This Project
    12	
    13	### 1. Evolutionary Algorithm-Based Hypothesis Generation (MOOSE-Chem)
    14	
    15	| Aspect | Detail |
    16	|--------|--------|
    17	| Source | Autonomous Agents Survey §3.2 |
    18	| Core Idea | Treat hypothesis generation as optimization: population → mutation → fitness evaluation → selection |
    19	| Mapping | Our `generate_with_docking_guidance()` already implements this cycle |
    20	| Status | ✅ IMPLEMENTED (H002) |
    21	
    22	### 2. Agent-as-a-Judge for Retrosynthesis (LARC)
    23	
    24	| Aspect | Detail |
    25	|--------|--------|
    26	| Source | Autonomous Agents Survey §4.2 / Chemistry Agents |
    27	| Core Idea | LLM evaluates retrosynthetic routes for feasibility; rule coverage determines quality |
    28	| Mapping | Our `score_route_quality()` implements route scoring |
    29	| Status | ✅ IMPLEMENTED (H012) |
    30	
    31	### 3. Tool Augmentation Pattern (ChemCrow)
    32	
    33	| Aspect | Detail |
    34	|--------|--------|
    35	| Source | Autonomous Agents Survey §4.2 / Coscientist |
    36	| Core Idea | 18+ specialized chemistry tools integrated under LLM orchestration |
    37	| Mapping | Our tool suite: identify_target, generate, dock, plan_synthesis, evaluate, run_pipeline |
    38	| Status | ✅ IMPLEMENTED |
    39	
    40	### 4. Self-Correction / Iterative Refinement (Coscientist)
    41	
